endue.formats Apple disk image and file system readers (lib/apple)

These readers were written for endue Desk from Apple's published specifications and from Apple's
own BSD-licensed reference decoder. No code was taken or followed from apfs-fuse, libfsapfs,
libfshfs, the Linux hfsplus or apfs drivers, afsctool, or any other source under the GPL or the
LGPL.

Sources followed

* Apple Technical Note TN1150, "HFS Plus Volume Format", Apple Developer documentation: the volume
  header, HFS wrappers, the B-tree files (catalog, extents overflow, attributes), catalog records,
  hard links through the private metadata folders, and symbolic links (hfs.js, hfs-btree.js,
  hfs-fork.js, hfs-catalog.js).

* Apple File System Reference, Apple Developer documentation
  (https://developer.apple.com/support/downloads/Apple-File-System-Reference.pdf): object headers
  and their Fletcher-64 checksums, the container superblock and checkpoints, object maps, B-tree
  nodes, volume superblocks, inodes, directory records, extents and extended attributes (apfs.js,
  apfs-object.js, apfs-fs.js).

* The UDIF layout (the "koly" trailer, the XML property list's "blkx" block tables, "mish" chunk
  tables and their chunk types) and the Apple Partition Map, as documented publicly, checked against
  images made with hdiutil (udif.js, chunks.js, plist.js, apm.js). ADC follows its public
  description (adc.js). decmpfs follows the attribute and resource-fork layouts macOS writes,
  checked by writing files through the public xattr calls and reading them back through the kernel
  (decmpfs.js; tests/apple/compress.py).

* LZFSE and LZVN: Apple's reference implementation, https://github.com/lzfse/lzfse
  (lzfse_decode_base.c, lzfse_fse.h, lzfse_fse.c, lzvn_decode_base.c, lzfse_internal.h), followed
  for lzfse.js, fse.js and lzvn.js under the BSD 3-clause licence below.

